    "hints": [
      "Find where 2x² − 8 changes sign between 0 and 3.",
      "2x² − 8 = 2(x − 2)(x + 2) is negative for 0 ≤ x < 2 and positive for 2 < x ≤ 3. Split the integral at x = 2, using 8 − 2x² on the first part.",
      "The integral of 8 − 2x² from 0 to 2 is 32/3 and the integral of 2x² − 8 from 2 to 3 is 14/3. Add them."
    ],
    "solution": [
